firebase/php-jwt 6.11.1
=======================

Vendored (source-only, no Composer runtime) from:
  https://github.com/firebase/php-jwt/releases/tag/v6.11.1

Vendored on: 2026-07-01
Licence:     BSD-3-Clause (see LICENSE)
PHP require: ^8.0 (project runs 8.4) — depends only on ext-openssl, ext-json,
             ext-mbstring (all present on Dreamhost shared hosting).

Files vendored under src/ (7 files):
  JWT.php                             — encode()/decode(), alg allow-listing via Key
  Key.php                             — (keyMaterial, algorithm) pair — the alg pin
  JWK.php                             — parseKeySet()/parseKey() for JWKS consumers
  BeforeValidException.php            — nbf/iat-in-future
  ExpiredException.php                — exp-in-past
  SignatureInvalidException.php       — bad signature
  JWTExceptionWithPayloadInterface.php— implemented by the two payload exceptions

Files DELIBERATELY NOT vendored:
  CachedKeySet.php  — pulls in psr/cache + psr/http-client + psr/http-factory,
                      none of which are needed (SIGNula serves its own JWKS from
                      tblSettings; it never fetches a remote JWKS). JWT::getKey()
                      guards it with `instanceof CachedKeySet`, which safely
                      evaluates to false when the class is absent (verified), so
                      omitting it changes no behaviour for our single-Key /
                      Key-array decode paths.

⚠️ SECURITY MAINTENANCE: this is security-critical crypto. Track upstream
   advisories at https://github.com/firebase/php-jwt/security/advisories and the
   GHSA feed, and bump this vendored copy when a fixed release ships. Record the
   new version here and in _docs/setup/SECURITY_SETUP.md.

How it is loaded (no Composer autoload in prod):
  web/private_html/security/JwtLibLoader.php require_once's these files
  explicitly (with file_exists() guards) in dependency order. The project-owned
  facade web/private_html/security/Jwt.php is the ONLY class the rest of the
  codebase calls — Firebase\JWT\* is never referenced directly outside the
  loader/facade/KeyManager.
